WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:03.420
All right, helpsters, our goal is to help me

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.550
and Grandma Gracie have a picnic.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:07.210
Now who's got an idea?

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:07.930
Huh?

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:08.430
Huh?

00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:11.190
You will need something to sit on at the park, perhaps

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.130
a picnic blanket.

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:16.000
Ah, I hear it and I like it.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:16.500
Me too.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.690
So that's job one.

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:20.460
Get a picnic blanket for the park.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.480
All right, what else?

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:26.370
To carry all the food and drink you will need a picnic basket.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:31.140
Yeah, we do, and that makes job two, find a picnic basket.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.150
Once we have a basket, you're going

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.340
to need to pack your lunches in it.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:38.940
Scatter, you always come up with the most delicious ideas.

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.000
Job three, pack a picnic lunch.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.890
Grandma Gracie, we have our plan.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:46.230
All right.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.960
(SINGING) We got the plan, got the plan.

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.050
We figured it out.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:50.880
We've got the plan.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:52.980
What happens when we've got the plan?

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.890
We give a happy shout just 'cause we can.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:57.000
Whoo.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.390
That's very satisfying.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:00:58.890
Yes, it is.

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:01.590
Lovely work, ladies, and good news.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.780
I have found some picnic blankets.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:04.360
Come along.

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:04.860
All right.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:05.370
Come along.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:05.870
OK.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:08.070
Let's step lively.

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:11.842
I just finished giving the picnic blankets a fresh wash.

00:01:11.842 --> 00:01:12.606
[BUZZ]

00:01:12.606 --> 00:01:14.280
Oh, and there they are.

00:01:14.280 --> 00:01:15.150
Done.

00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:17.210
This is exciting.

00:01:17.210 --> 00:01:18.600
Ha ha.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:19.330
Oh, no.

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:22.710
The red blanket has shrunk.

00:01:22.710 --> 00:01:25.740
Not to worry, I have a yellow blanket.

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:26.940
Yellow is good.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.350
And here it is.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:28.950
Yeah.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:29.640
Oh, no.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:31.500
The yellow blanket has shrunk.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.380
Not to worry, I've got another red one.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:36.360
Which has shrunk.

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.700
They've all shrunk.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.980
I've ruined the picnic.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.520
Wait, I have an idea.

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.410
What if you sew the tiny square blankets together

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:48.870
to make one big square blanket?

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.510
Whoa, Grandma.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.270
And I know the sequence we should put the squares in.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:55.620
Sequence?

00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:58.290
It means the order in which things happen.

00:01:58.290 --> 00:02:00.750
Grandma, please follow my commands, OK?

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:01.290
OK.

00:02:01.290 --> 00:02:01.890
OK.

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:07.230
First, place a red square on the table.

00:02:07.230 --> 00:02:12.570
Next, place a yellow square next to the red square.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:17.550
Next, place a red square next to that yellow square.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:22.650
Last, place a yellow square next to that red square.

00:02:22.650 --> 00:02:23.910
Very nice.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:24.850
Thank you.

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:26.830
OK, now we can do the next row.

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:29.280
So first place a red square--

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.410
Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait a minute.

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:34.050
If we're going to do the same thing over and over,

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:36.180
then we can just loop and you don't

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:38.040
need to say all those steps.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:39.060
What's loop?

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:41.910
Loop means to do something again and again.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:46.500
So we need four rows, so we'll loop three more time.

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.874
Allow me.

00:02:48.874 --> 00:02:51.240
There we go.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:52.446
Oh.

00:02:52.446 --> 00:02:54.740
I know what I'm doing here.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:55.380
OK.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:58.060
Don't worry, Grandma, he's really good.

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:58.560
OK.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:02:59.550
He is.

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:02.040
And finished.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:04.992
Bravo.

00:03:04.992 --> 00:03:06.135
This is fabulous.

00:03:06.135 --> 00:03:07.860
Look at that.

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:10.740
Find a picnic blanket for the park, check.

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:11.970
One job done.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:14.100
Two more to go.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:15.740
Cody, Grandma Gracie?

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:16.240
Yeah?

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:18.430
I'm ready for you in the other room now.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:19.840
OK, we're on our way, Heart.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:20.970
Come on, Grandma.

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:23.700
I shall stay behind and make sure this blanket does not

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:24.520
get shrunk.

00:03:24.520 --> 00:03:26.570
I found your basket.

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:27.380
Ah ha.

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:32.170
Oh, Heart, I'm so sorry.

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.690
I should have been clearer with my instructions.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:38.450
That picnic basket is way too big.

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:41.530
This is not a picnic basket.

00:03:41.530 --> 00:03:42.775
It's not?

00:03:42.775 --> 00:03:46.570
No, this is a hot air balloon basket

00:03:46.570 --> 00:03:48.640
to get to the picnic basket.

00:03:48.640 --> 00:03:49.140
Wow.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:50.642
Care to join me?

00:03:50.642 --> 00:03:53.474
Well, sure.

00:03:53.474 --> 00:03:57.880
So, uh, by the way, Heart, where we going?

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.150
Denmark.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:03:59.650
Wow.

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:01.610
Denmark?

00:04:01.610 --> 00:04:02.730
Thank you, Heart.

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:04.340
Of course.

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:07.250
Oh, hi, nice lady.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:08.840
Hi, basket maker Berta.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:09.800
Hi, Heart.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:11.240
Welcome to Denmark.

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:12.270
Here's your basket.

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:14.030
Thank you.

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:16.660
Find a picnic basket, check.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:19.970
Two jobs done, one more to go.

00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:23.710
OK, Scatter, here's the basket ready for packing.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:27.280
And here's your food ready for eating.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:28.870
Oh, that looks scrumptious.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:30.734
I'll put them in the basket.

00:04:30.734 --> 00:04:31.670
Here you go.

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:33.932
Thank you.

00:04:33.932 --> 00:04:34.432
OK.

00:04:37.390 --> 00:04:38.720
Oh, no.

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:40.750
The lid won't close.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:43.270
Picnic canceled.

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:45.200
Well, wait a minute, buddy bud.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:47.050
Let's debug.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:47.670
Debug?

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:48.220
Hm-huh.

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.050
Oh, we call problems bugs.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:52.190
Yeah, and when we find and fix the problem,

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:54.600
we call it debugging.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:58.280
Well, we already have found the problem, the top won't close.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:00.173
So how do we fix it?

00:05:00.173 --> 00:05:00.860
Hm?

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:04.190
What if we put the food in a different way?

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:07.038
Yes, so it doesn't take up so much space.

00:05:07.038 --> 00:05:07.580
That's right.

00:05:07.580 --> 00:05:09.705
Hey, Scatter, can you take everything out of there,

00:05:09.705 --> 00:05:11.990
please?

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:15.910
First, put one water bottle inside the basket.

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:17.030
Na na.

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:20.420
Next, put the other water bottle next to that one.

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:21.700
Na na.

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:25.670
Then place the sandwiches on top of the water bottle.

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:28.640
Then place the carrot sticks next to the water bottles.

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:29.840
Na na.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:33.855
Last, put the plates and napkins on top of the carrot sticks,

00:05:33.855 --> 00:05:34.355
and?

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.260
If fits.

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:40.610
Pack a picnic lunch, check.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:43.660
All the jobs are done.

